New Product Development Management takes the entire new product development process as its central thread, covering the economic and managerial activities involved in bringing a new product from ideation and concept generation through design, engineering, manufacturing, and commercialization. Issues addressed include new product strategy, organizing for new product development, and fostering creativity. The course is divided into eight modules:
(1) Overview of New Product Management;
(2) New Product Development Strategy;
(3) New Product Development Organization;
(4) The New Product Development Process;
(5) Concept Development for New Products;
(6) Technology Development for New Products;
(7) Commercial Development of New Products;
(8) New Product Development in Practice—Stage-Gate Management.

