This course will cover the fundamental principles and techniques of modern data mining and machine learning, including supervised learning techniques (such as classification and prediction) and unsupervised learning techniques (such as pattern discovery, dimensionality reduction, and clustering). The course will present practical business cases, and students will have the opportunity to learn and apply either R or Python to these cases. Specifically, the course will include the following topics:


Basic concepts of machine learning;

Supervised learning techniques (regression and classification methods);

Unsupervised learning techniques (pattern discovery, dimensionality reduction, clustering, and association rules);

Machine learning packages in R or Python.

