This course covers the fundamental principles of databases, the SQL language, operations of database management systems, enterprise data management methods, and the development of intelligent agents enhanced by data.

The main topics include:


Principles and operations of databases, including relational database theory and the standard relational database language SQL;

Database system management, including database security, database integrity, and related management mechanisms;

Enterprise data management methods, including database design methodologies, normalization theory for relational database design, and enterprise data integration approaches;

Big data management technologies, including data warehousing, OLAP, distributed storage, and distributed computing;

AI application development with “Database + LLM”, focusing on building data- and knowledge-driven intelligent question-answering systems based on databases, RAG techniques, and large-model application platforms.

This course primarily focuses on the theories and methodologies of data science and the utilization of data science packages in Python. The core content includes:

(1) Data analysis with the advanced operations of NumPy and Pandas;

(2) The principles and implementation of classical machine learning methods, including classification, regression, clustering, dimensionality reduction, recommendation algorithms, topic models, etc.;

(3) The principles and implementation of classical deep learning methods (i.e., various types of classical neural networks);

(4) The application of data analysis methods in practical scenarios.

The content consists of two parts:

I. Introduction to fundamental concepts and knowledge of probability theory, covering the axiomatic definition of probability, random variables and their distributions, multivariate random variables, numerical characteristics of random variables, the law of large numbers, and the central limit theorem;
II. Introduction to fundamental concepts and knowledge of mathematical statistics, covering populations and samples, statistics and their sampling distributions, parameter estimation, and hypothesis testing.

Linear models are an important class of statistical models, with rich theory and wide-ranging applications. This course systematically introduces the fundamental theory, methods, and applications of linear models, as well as their extensions to high-dimensional and big data settings. The main topics include:




General methods for parameter estimation, hypothesis testing, and interval estimation in linear models;




Applications of the general theory, including linear regression models, analysis of variance (ANOVA) models, analysis of covariance (ANCOVA) models, and mixed-effects models;




Recent research developments in high-dimensional linear models.
